<header><p class="st-kicker">protectorate · Arabia and the Gulf</p><h1 class="st-title">Federation of South Arabia</h1><p class="st-meta">1962 CE – 1967 CE · capital Al Ittihad</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Britain's last attempt to build a friendly state around Aden, which collapsed under nationalist insurgency in 1967.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>In April 1962 the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/federation-of-arab-emirates-of-the-south">Federation of Arab Emirates of the South</a> was renamed the Federation of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-arabia">South Arabia</a>. In January 1963 the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/colony-of-aden">Colony of Aden</a> joined as the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/state-of-aden">State of Aden</a>, despite opposition from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aden">Aden's</a> trade unions and nationalists, and more <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protectorate">protectorate</a> states joined in the following years.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The federation was ruled by sultans, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emir">emirs</a> and sheikhs with British advisers, and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-kingdom">Britain</a> kept its military base at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aden">Aden</a>. In December 1963 a grenade attack on the High Commissioner at Aden airport led to a state of emergency. Two rival movements, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/national-liberation-front-south-yemen">National Liberation Front</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/front-for-the-liberation-of-occupied-south-yemen">FLOSY</a>, fought the British and each other in Aden and the Radfan mountains.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 1966 <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-kingdom">Britain</a> announced it would leave without a defence agreement. In 1967 the federal army and states collapsed as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/national-liberation-front-south-yemen">National Liberation Front</a> took over; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> withdrew on 29 November 1967 and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/south-yemen">South Yemen</a> became independent.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/federation-of-south-arabia.jpg" alt="Federation of South Arabia" width="320" height="160"><figcaption>Image: R-41 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_Federation_of_South_Arabia.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1962 CE – 1967 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>protectorate</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>colonial</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Al Ittihad</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Arabic</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/yemen">Yemen</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>South Arabian Federation</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1964&amp;focus=federation-of-south-arabia" aria-label="Federation of South Arabia on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5993 1607 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Federation of South Arabia lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M6313 1863L6236 1957M6313 1863L6313 1863M6313 1863L4997 651M6313 1863L6236 1957M6313 1863L6247 1946M6313 1863L6252 1934M6313 1863L6256 1915M6313 1863L6252 1934M6313 1863L6226 1924M6313 1863L6273 1938M6313 1863L6242 1941M6313 1863L6272 1894M6313 1863L6273 1901M6313 1863L6223 1933M6313 1863L6222 1967M6313 1863L6224 1932M6313 1863L6225 1924M6313 1863L6262 1915M6313 1863L6319 1914"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6236 1957h0M6313 1863h0M4997 651h0M6236 1957h0M6247 1946h0M6252 1934h0M6256 1915h0M6252 1934h0M6226 1924h0M6273 1938h0M6242 1941h0M6272 1894h0M6273 1901h0M6223 1933h0M6222 1967h0M6224 1932h0M6225 1924h0M6262 1915h0M6319 1914h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6313 1863h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6313 1863h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=1964&amp;focus=federation-of-south-arabia">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcap